00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.460
Process automation can
help with manual task.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.210
But some of that manual
work done each day

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.120
requires taking data from a
document, like an invoice,

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.770
and inputting it
into another data

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.723
source or a disparate system.

00:00:24.723 --> 00:00:26.640
This takes up valuable
time that could be used

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.680
to focus on high-impact work.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.560
AppSheet combines the power of
no-code development with Google

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.500
Cloud's state-of-the-art
Document AI to automatically

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.420
extract and validate your data--

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.440
like invoices,
receipts, et cetera--

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.350
making your workflows
more efficient and free

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:44.310
from guesswork, all while
keeping the human in the loop.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.620
You can think of this
intelligent document processing

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:47.940
functionality like a layer.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.380
It sits on top of
the automations

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.422
you can build currently,
creating a different way

00:00:51.422 --> 00:00:53.670
to trigger automation events
or showcase information

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.790
in your applications from
unstructured document data.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:00.030
Let's explore an example
of how this is done.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.578
Ben works on a finance team for
a large transportation firm.

00:01:03.578 --> 00:01:05.370
Each week, he receives
hundreds of pictures

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.140
of receipts and PDFs
of invoices that

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.450
need to be processed for
reimbursements and payments

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.190
to various teams
across the country.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:13.350
These are time sensitive.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.517
He needs a way to keep up
with the increasing number

00:01:15.517 --> 00:01:16.830
of documents sent his way.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:19.440
He has access to both Google
Workspace and AppSheet,

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.360
allowing a fast
path to a solution,

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.950
even though he's not a coder.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.990
By creating and connecting
designated folders

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.387
in his Google Drive account
to his AppSheet applications,

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.220
he'll be able to upload
pictures of receipts

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.180
and PDFs of invoices to perform
a designated series of actions.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.430
For reimbursements, he can
trigger both the extraction

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.890
of the data and an approval
request notification

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.530
to his manager, all by
uploading invoice and receipt

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.140
documents to the
preselected Drive folder.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.370
If he really wants to
take it to the next level,

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:47.130
he can refine the
application experience

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:48.840
that houses
automation so that he

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.820
can perform this action
from a mobile device

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.160
while he's working with
the teams in the field.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.190
These benefits don't just need
to apply to those in finance.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:57.840
Anyone on your team
can create impact

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.015
by removing the time spent
on document processing

00:02:00.015 --> 00:02:02.520
with no-code platforms
like AppSheet.

